From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:30:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s800x: Measured motion sensor mount
 matrices for the iPhones

Held still in six poses on an iPhone 6s Plus (N66), the AOP's raw
accelerometer reads, in g (mean of 14 samples each):

  screen up                      0.033   0.006  -0.958
  screen down                   -0.013  -0.006   1.052
  portrait, home button down     0.002  -0.930  -0.316
  portrait, home button up      -0.001   0.974  -0.180
  landscape, home button right  -0.938   0.032  -0.307
  landscape, home button left    0.939  -0.004  -0.325

(z of about -0.3 in the upright poses is the phone leaning back.) The
axes are the device's, x right, y up, z out of the screen, with gravity's
sign. Of the 48 signed axis permutations, diag(1, 1, -1) puts every pose
where iio-sensor-proxy expects it (normal, bottom-up, right-up, left-up,
face-up, face-down); the next best is 3.75 g^2 worse. It is the iPad 5's
measured matrix, although the ADT's accel-orientation turns the 6s Plus's
sensor 90 degrees against the iPad's: the firmware reports on the device's
axes, so the matrix holds for every A9 iPhone, not only this board.

The gyroscope is the same MPU6800. During the turns between poses its
rates match the change of the accelerometer's gravity vector best with no
remapping (dg/dt = -w x g over 26 sample pairs: identity fits best of the
48), e.g. +1.6 rad/s about y while the phone flipped over through +x, and
+z while gravity swung from -x to +y. At rest it reads under 0.03 rad/s.
Give it the identity matrix so the device frame is stated.

Drop the note that the AOP's matrix is not measured yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
index 3498ce5ea..3b9b46dfc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
@@ -135,8 +135,7 @@ fuel-gauge {
 
 /*
  * Apple's A9 iPhone AOP firmware (aopfw-s8000aop) serves the accelerometer,
- * gyroscope and pressure sensor. Its mount-matrix has not been measured on
- * a phone yet, so the sensors report in the AOP's own frame.
+ * gyroscope and pressure sensor.
  */
 &aop {
 	firmware-name = "apple/aop-s8000.bin", "apple/aop-s8000-ext.bin";
@@ -146,3 +145,20 @@ &aop {
 &aop_mbox {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * Measured on an iPhone 6s Plus: the firmware reports on the device's axes
+ * (x right, y up, z out of the screen) with the accelerometer giving
+ * gravity's sign, as on the iPad 5, so the matrices hold for every A9 iPhone.
+ */
+&aop_accel {
+	mount-matrix = "1", "0", "0",
+		       "0", "1", "0",
+		       "0", "0", "-1";
+};
+
+&aop_gyro {
+	mount-matrix = "1", "0", "0",
+		       "0", "1", "0",
+		       "0", "0", "1";
+};
